#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-desks: every Claude on a KDE desktop of its own (the desktop manager).

Desktop 1 is yours and is never created, removed, renamed, ended or resumed here. Every other desktop this tool
makes belongs to one Claude: its Konsole fills that desktop until something else opens on it. The slots are only where
windows start; the zone engine tiles them afterwards, and the Claude is an ordinary tiled window with no reserved
quadrant. The Claude hub is a popup on no desktop (claude-hub).

A Claude desktop never disappears by itself: the only way one is ended is through the hub (or `end`). When its Claude
stops (its window was closed, it quit, it crashed) the desktop stays, marked stopped, and `resume` brings the Claude
back; only `end` removes it.

Besides yours and the Claudes', a few special desktops exist, each with a state file under
~/.local/state/claude-hub/ (a launcher desktop, an aux desktop): they hold one app, no Claude is put on them, and
`end` and `resume` refuse them. Your own extra desktops are called Main Desktop N, made right after your last desktop
(`main-desktop new`) and listed by id in ~/.local/state/claude-hub/main-desktops.json (CLAUDE_HUB_MAIN_DESKTOPS_FILE).
A Claude or a Codex can neither make nor close one (exit 7).

The registry is ~/.local/state/claude-hub/desktops.json, {"boot": "<boot id>", "desktops": [entry, ...]}, one entry
per Claude desktop, rewritten atomically under a lock. `boot` is the id of the boot that wrote it
(/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id): a pid means something only in the boot that handed it out, so a registry of an
earlier boot is read as if no entry had a Konsole or a process, in memory only.

claude-desks whoami [--json]         the calling Claude's desktop: "<id> <number> <name>"; exit 1 and nothing printed
                                           when it has none
  claude-desks main-desktop new|list|close [--stop] [--json]
                                           new: a Main Desktop right after your last one; list: your desktops in KDE's
                                           order; close <id>: ask each ordinary window that lives only there to close
                                           (none is killed; Cancel on a question keeps the desktop). Exit 0 done, 1
                                           refused or failed, 3 kept or stopped, 7 a Claude or a Codex asked
  claude-desks place --desktop <id|number> --slot claude|right|center (--caption TEXT | --pid N) [--confirm]
                         [--screen primary]
                                           put a window on that desktop in that slot (the whole of it, the right half,
                                           or centred at its own size), on the screen being watched. Idempotent; exit 4
                                           = KWin ran it and no window matched; --confirm makes "ran but never
                                           reported" exit 6. A Claude places only on its own desktop (exit 1 for
                                           another), unless CLAUDE_HUB_DESKTOP_SWITCH_OK=1
  claude-desks claim --desktop <id|number> (--pid N | --class CLASS --marker TEXT) [--ttl S] [--grace S]
                         [--deadline EPOCH]
                                           before opening a window: the next window of that process (or app) opens on
                                           that desktop, never first on your screen. Prints {"id", "seen"}; exit 3 =
                                           not seen: `place` still moves it afterwards
  claude-desks aux-desktop open|close|status [--json]
  claude-desks unclaim <id>            a claim whose window never came, dropped (they also expire)
  claude-desks goto <id|number> [--no-focus]
                                           switch there and focus that desktop's Claude
  claude-desks new <account> [--attach ID] [--stay] [--model M] [--effort E]
                       [--title TEXT] [--message TEXT]
                                           a new desktop at the end with a Claude's Konsole on it (--attach: a running
                                           background Claude instead of a new one;
                                           --message: the first message the Claude is sent)
  claude-desks resume <id|number>      that desktop's Claude back in a window on it, and go there
  claude-desks end <id|number>         the only end of a Claude desktop: stop its Claude, close every window only on
                                           it, remove it, forget it; one line says what happened
  claude-desks adopt [--session ID] [--goto] [--json] [--dry-run]
                                           running Claudes without a desktop get one; their Konsole moves there.
                                           Nothing is restarted
  claude-desks remove <id|number>      gone (exit 2): a Claude desktop ends only through `end`
  claude-desks sync [--json]           the upkeep of every refresh: rename desktops after their Claude, mark a gone
                                           Claude stopped (nothing is removed)
  claude-desks watch [--once]          the desktop service (claude-desktops.service): a look every second, every
                                           account's sessions every 2 s, sync after each; writes the rows the popup
                                           draws in hub.json and answers on org.claudehub.Desktops
  claude-desks active [--json]         the pid of the window you have focused, asked of KWin; exit 1 = none, 3 = no
                                           answer
  claude-desks focus --caption TEXT    raise the first window whose title contains TEXT (prints focused|switched|gone)
  claude-desks refocus <window id>     give you back that window (an `active --json` id) after something took the
                                           keyboard
  claude-desks sticky [--json]         the screens in front of you, each `sticky` (it keeps desktop 1 while the others
                                           switch desktops) or `switches`
  claude-desks sticky <screen> on|off  mark one sticky or not
  claude-desks list [--json]
"""
